# The Atlas — Spatial Ground Succession Instrument

**BitPangea · The Atlas · Spatial Ground**  
**Instrument Type:** Succession Instrument  
**Creator Period:** Day #122 · September 26, 2026  
**Status:** COMPLETE — READY FOR ADOPTION  
**Institutional Home:** The Atlas  
**Successor Office:** Atlas Adoption Authority — Successor Office  
**World-Space Design Authority Transferred:** None after canonical instance adoption  
**Canonical World-Space Effect:** None

---

## 1. Purpose

This Instrument establishes continuity of lawful Atlas authority after the Creator Period without transferring or recreating the Creator's exhausted power to design canonical World-space.

The governing principle is:

> **Succession transfers the office and never the design.**

What has been adopted is inherited as fact.

What was never adopted is not silently inherited as hidden authority.

---

## 2. Successor Office

The continuing Atlas adoption authority shall be exercised after the Creator Period by the:

> **Atlas Adoption Authority — Successor Office**

This is an office within The Atlas.

It is not a new constitutional institution.

The particular person or organization serving that office may change without changing the office or Spatial Ground canon.

---

## 3. Source of Authority

The Successor Office derives its authority only from:

1. this recorded Succession Instrument;
2. applicable constitutional sources;
3. adopted Atlas governance that is subordinate to those sources.

Authority SHALL NOT arise from:

- possession of canonical records;
- repository ownership;
- private keys;
- infrastructure control;
- organizational continuity;
- self-declaration;
- majority support;
- implementation control.

---

## 4. What Survives the Creator

The following survive permanently:

- every recorded Adoption Act;
- every recorded canonical status determination;
- the adopted canonical World-space instance;
- the fact and content of recorded corrections;
- the continuing powers expressly assigned to the Atlas adoption authority.

Nothing unrecorded survives as authority.

Personal memory is never a governing source.

---

## 5. Exhaustion of World-Space Design Authority

Upon adoption of the canonical World-space instance:

> **the authority to choose which Survey space is BitPangea World-space is exhausted.**

Accordingly, the Successor Office receives:

```text
NO AUTHORITY
```

to:

- redesign World-space;
- replace World-space with a preferred alternative;
- expand World-space;
- contract World-space;
- move the canonical limit;
- create a second canonical World-space;
- treat technological improvement as authority to redesign.

The canonical instance is inherited as fact.

---

## 6. Continuing Successor Powers

The Successor Office MAY:

1. adopt compatible revisions to Requirements;
2. adopt compatible revisions to the Spatial Ground Specification;
3. adopt revisions to shared Atlas architectural doctrine;
4. designate successor normative representations on proof of semantic equivalence;
5. replace a formal model on proof of continuity of canonical meaning;
6. recognize or withdraw recognition of Stewards;
7. decide factually which artifact was adopted where records conflict;
8. accept compatible FSF lineage / dependency certifications;
9. approve scope clarification or change where permitted and properly routed;
10. correct defective records under the same correction standard that governed during the Creator Period.

Each exercise of authority SHALL be recorded.

---

## 7. Prohibited Successor Powers

The Successor Office SHALL NOT:

- reinterpret canonical membership;
- infer authority from undocumented Creator intent;
- alter World-space because a different design is preferable;
- amend constitutional sources by Atlas action;
- treat stewardship as governance authority;
- treat implementation correctness as adoption;
- treat publication as adoption;
- treat use or popularity as adoption;
- use a private key as proof of institutional authority.

---

## 8. Record Correction

The Successor Office may correct a defective record only where correction restores what the adopted record demonstrably required.

Correction SHALL use:

- the adopted primary artifact;
- the Adoption Act;
- the governing Requirements;
- the governing Specification;
- preserved evidence.

Correction SHALL NOT use free-standing recollection of Creator intent.

---

## 9. Constitutional Defect

If an adopted Spatial Ground record is later demonstrated to violate a superior constitutional constraint:

1. the matter SHALL return constitutionally upstream;
2. any Ground correction SHALL be the narrowest correction necessary to restore conformity;
3. if the conforming correction is uniquely determined by the record and superior constraint, the Successor Office MAY record that correction;
4. if two or more materially distinct conforming cures remain possible, the Successor Office SHALL NOT choose among them under ordinary succession authority;
5. such discretionary curative design must be resolved by a superior authority or by a separately adopted instrument expressly conferring that narrow power.

This Instrument intentionally does **not** confer open-ended curative design authority.

---

## 10. Requirements and Specification Revision

Requirements and Specification remain revisable after the Creator Period only where canonical meaning is preserved.

A successor revision SHALL:

- identify its predecessor;
- state the authority exercised;
- demonstrate compatibility;
- preserve predecessor records;
- not alter adopted World-space membership.

---

## 11. Formal Model Replacement

A formal model may be replaced only on proof that the successor model preserves canonical Ground meaning.

Model replacement is implementation/formalism succession.

It is not World-space redesign.

---

## 12. Primary Representation Supersession

A primary representation may be superseded where:

- equivalence is decidable;
- equivalence is demonstrated;
- the predecessor is preserved;
- the successor is explicitly designated by recorded act.

If semantic equivalence cannot be established, the proposed successor SHALL NOT replace the canonical instance representation.

---

## 13. Steward Recognition

The Successor Office may recognize Spatial Ground Stewards under `SG_Stewardship_Instrument.md`.

Recognition confers preservation responsibility only.

The Successor Office MAY itself also perform stewardship functions, but the roles remain institutionally distinct.

---

## 14. Conflicting Records

When two records both claim canonical status, the Successor Office acts only as finder of fact.

The question is:

> **Which artifact was actually adopted?**

The question is not:

> **Which artifact would produce the better World?**

Evidence may include:

- Adoption Acts;
- integrity records;
- repository history;
- preservation manifests;
- Steward evidence;
- Chronicle records;
- other contemporaneous institutional evidence.

Established canon prevails during the dispute.

---

## 15. Authority of Keys and Infrastructure

Keys authenticate acts.

Keys do not create authority.

Infrastructure carries records.

Infrastructure does not create authority.

Therefore:

- loss of a key does not abolish the office;
- possession of a key does not constitute the office;
- transfer of hosting does not transfer the office;
- repository ownership does not transfer the office.

---

## 16. Power Vacuum

If no person or institution is serving the Successor Office:

1. canonical Ground remains unchanged;
2. adopted acts remain in force;
3. Stewards and Custodians in Fact may continue preservation;
4. no preservation actor acquires adoption authority;
5. no adoption-class act may occur until lawful authority is constituted.

A vacancy never opens World-space for redesign.

---

## 17. Successor Appointment Mechanism

The office-holder SHOULD be designated by a recorded Atlas governance act that:

- identifies the office-holder;
- cites this Instrument;
- identifies the effective date;
- identifies any term or succession trigger;
- preserves the institutional distinction between office and person.

The appointment mechanism may evolve.

The powers of the office may not silently expand through that evolution.

---

## 18. No Authority Personality

The identity of Spatial Ground canon is independent of the identity of the office-holder.

Succession therefore preserves:

> **canon, not authority personality.**

The office-holder may change.

The World does not.

---

## 19. If the Creator Period Ends Before Instance Adoption

This Instrument is designed on the expectation that the canonical World-space instance will be adopted during the Creator Period.

If the Creator Period ends before that adoption occurs:

- World-space design authority SHALL NOT be presumed transferred;
- the Successor Office SHALL NOT infer that authority from this Instrument;
- the unresolved design authority must be expressly conferred by a valid superior or contemporaneously authorized instrument before it can be exercised.

This clause prevents accidental inheritance of unexercised design power.

---

## 20. Recording Requirement

Every successor act SHALL identify:

- the acting office;
- the authority invoked;
- the artifact or rule affected;
- the predecessor where applicable;
- evidence of conformity/equivalence where required;
- the effective institutional status.

Unrecorded successor intent has no canonical effect.

---

## 21. Supremacy and Subordination

This Instrument is subordinate to every applicable constitutional source.

If a constitutional source controls a succession matter differently, the constitutional source governs.

This Instrument SHALL be interpreted to preserve constitutional subordination.

---

## 22. Adoption Clause

This Instrument becomes governing only upon a recorded adoption act by the Creator acting as Atlas adoption authority during the Creator Period.

Until adopted, it is a completed candidate instrument.

---

